Since this sounds like a beginner question, let me start by giving you
the standard layout for wishes:
[How many][blessed status][erodability][enchantment][name]

An example is: "3 blessed rustproof +3 darts".  Of course this is not a 
very good thing to wish for, but it shows the structure.  Your chances 
of getting the enchantment you wish for goes up as the enchantment goes 
up.  So if you can wish for a +8 whatever, but you won't get it, only a
+0 one.  +2 or +3 are normal choices.

A Wand of Wishing typically has three charges, but not always.  They can,
however, be recharged once.  Just in case you've happened to find a 
Wand of Wishing (1), your very first wish should be for something to
recharge your wand (which can then give you 3 more wishes).  The simplest
thing to wish for which can recharge a wand is a scroll of charghing (or
better yet, "3 blessed scrolls of charging").

A final point about wands of wishing is that you can squeeze one more wish 
out of them by zapping them repeatedly (a hundred times or so) once they 
get to 0 charges.  This destroys the wand, but give you one more wish (or 
a total of 7 (3, recharge, 3, squeeze out one more) out of a wand).

My own personal guideline is to wish for armor, and get weapons as a gift
from god by sacrificing at an alter.  In any case, I'll now repost my
standard list of things to wish for.  Quest artifacts are not high priority
since I never wish for them.  The exact order varies from game to game,
(for example, I might wish for "3 blessed scrolls of charging", but if
I've already found charging I'd much rather wish for a blessed magic 
marker which will let me write them) but it is significant that the top 
4 things on my list are armor.  (If I ever find an early wand of wishing,
I would definitely wish for all 4).

 High Priority
 -------------
 "blessed +2 gray dragon scale mail"
 "blessed rustproof +2 pair of speed boots"
 "blessed rustproof +2 gauntlets of power"
 "blessed +2 shield of reflection" (in 3.1.1 or later)
 "blessed amulet of life saving"
 "blessed wand of polymorph"
 "blessed bag of holding"
 "blessed magic marker"

 Medium Priority
 ---------------
 "blessed figurine of an Archon" (better than a sheild of reflection in 3.1.0)
 "blessed rustproof +2 Grayswandir" -> good against major demons
 "blessed rustproof +2 Mjollnir" -> Great if you're a Valkyrie
 "blessed rustproof +2 Vorpal Blade" -> good for a quick kill
 "blessed +2 broadsword named Stormbringer" -> tough to control
 "blessed +2 long sword named Excalibur" -> protects against level drain
    -> many more weapons, but easier to get them by sacrificing
 "blessed platinum yendorian exress card (if Neutral)"
 "3 blessed scrolls of charging" (if not Neutral, and can't write it))
 "blessed tinning kit" (makes blessed tins)
 "3 blessed potions of gain ability"
 "3 blessed scrolls of genocide"
 "blessed ring of levitation" (you'll probably find one before endgame)
 "blessed ring of teleport control" (if you got teleport without control)
 "blessed luckstone" (get it in the mines instead of wishing)

Low Priority
------------
 "blessed amulet of magical breathing"
 "blessed rustproof +2 water walking boots"
 "blessed rustproof +2 helm of brilliance"
 "blessed rustproof +2 helm of telepathy"
 "blessed rustproof +2 cloak of displacement"
 "blessed rustproof +2 Hawaiian shirt"
 "3 cursed scrolls of genocide" (caution is advised)
 "blessed spellbook of identify" -> or many other spell books
 "blessed rustproof +2 helm of opposite alignment"

